   "line": [
    "Nc3"
   ],
   "spoken": "The Four Knights Scotch — the knights come out, then d4. Not a boring beginner opening; it's popular at the highest level and dangerous for an imprecise Black."
  },
  {
   "ply": 6,
   "t": 70.5,
   "fen": "r1bqk1nr/pppp1ppp/2n5/2b1p3/4P3/2N2N2/PPPP1PPP/R1BQKB1R w KQkq - 4 4",
   "line": [
    "Bc5"
   ],
   "spoken": "The bishop to c5 is a well-known inaccuracy in this line."
  },
  {
   "ply": 7,
   "t": 89,
   "fen": "r1bqk1nr/pppp1ppp/2n5/2b1N3/4P3/2N5/PPPP1PPP/R1BQKB1R b KQkq - 0 4",
   "line": [
    "Nxe5"
   ],
   "spoken": "The knight takes on e5 — and don't fear the response Bxf2-check; it turns out to be essentially losing for Black."
  },
  {
   "ply": 8,
   "t": 104,
   "fen": "r1bqk1nr/pppp1ppp/8/2b1n3/4P3/2N5/PPPP1PPP/R1BQKB1R w KQkq - 0 5",
